Micha Pringle wrote:
> 
> 3. When storing loot, what is the best medium to store the loot in? A
> Sack? A Chest? do I need to lock a chest, or is leaving it unlocked
> going to keep monsters out of it? Does a sack work at all for storing
> loot for long periods?

Any container is fine. A closet is almost as good. Pushing a
boulder over a pile of stuff works well, except for giants
and engraving Elbereth is good insurance in any case. In a
pinch just pile stuff up and engrave Elbereth. A cursed item
on top will prevent your pets from moving stuff around. The
lowest level of Sokoban is a popular stash location since
you won't ever be there again except to manage your stash.

> 5. Why is praying lots bad? It seems from my experience that I WANT to
> boost my luck to a certain level (mostly to avoid crowning), pray,
> then zap away with my wands of create monster and sacrifice to appease
> my god before praying again.

Sac and pray when safe for spellbooks and favors. Just keep
sacrificing for weapons. Break that wand when it's down to
one charge. Curse your scrolls of create monster. If you are
nervous about summoning up several monsters at once, make a
boulder fort around the altar so only one monster at a time
can attack you and that monster has to stand on the altar.
You might even burn a safety square for the (m)mf you're
about to summon.
> 
> 6. What in your opinion is the best order to do areas before the
> Quest? I do, Sokoban, sometimes a bit deeper in the DoD, then the
> Gnomish Mines, Then FL (if I could find it), then Medusa's island,
> then the Castle, finally the Quest.

I find the mines allow my character to improve his AC best
and that is very important. A pick ax is a very helpful tool
and a few daggers for throwing can also usually be gained in
just one level of the mines. If I have infravision or the
first level of the mines is lit I'll probably try that
first. A good pet is a big help when tackling the mines
first. If I can get to Minetown the priest and the stores
are quite useful for developing a character. I prefer
Minetown, Sokoban and then mine's end.

Medusa is trivial if you have the right equipment. Ludious
and the castle are much more dangerous without reflection.
The castle is deep enough to generate the liche family so I
am most reluctant to go there without MR.
